[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Five Pounds Too Dear]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.36]Lesson 28 | 第28课
[00:02.68]Five pounds too dear | 5镑也太贵
[00:10.72]Why was even five pounds 'too dear' ? | 为什么连5英镑也“太贵”了？
[00:16.88]Small boats loaded with wares sped to the great liner as she was entering the harbour. | 一艘大客轮正驶进港口，装满货物的小船迅速向它驶来。
[00:23.63]Before she had anchored, the men from the boats had climbed on board | 大船还未抛锚，小船上的人就爬上了客轮，
[00:28.49]and the decks were soon covered with colourful rugs from Persia, | 甲板上很快摆满了波斯地毯、印度丝绸、
[00:33.30]silks from India, copper coffee pots, and beautiful handmade silverware. | 铜咖啡壶以及漂亮的手工银器。
[00:40.08]It was difficult not to be tempted. | 要想不动心是很困难的。
[00:43.30]Many of the tourists on board had begun bargaining with the tradesmen, | 船上的许多游客开始与商贩讨价还价，
[00:47.47]but I decided not to buy anything until I had disembarked. | 但我决定等上岸以后再买东西。
[00:53.56]I had no sooner got off the ship than I was assailed by a man who wanted to sell me a diamond ring. | 我刚下船，一个想卖给我钻石戒指的人便缠住了我。
[01:02.16]I had no intention of buying one, | 我无意购买，
[01:04.87]but I could not conceal the fact that I was impressed by the size of the diamonds. | 但钻石之大却给我留下了深刻的印象，我无法掩盖这一事实。
[01:11.44]Some of them were as big as marbles. | 有些钻石大如弹子球。
[01:14.63]The man went to great lengths to prove that the diamonds were real. | 那人竭力想证明这些钻石是真货。
[01:19.90]As we were walking past a shop, he held a diamond firmly against the window and made a deep impression in the glass. | 走过一家商店时，他将一颗钻石使劲抵在橱窗上，在玻璃上划出一道深深的痕迹。
[01:28.90]It took me over half an hour to get rid of him. | 我花了半个多小时才摆脱了他。
[01:32.93]The next man to approach me was selling expensive pens and watches. | 接下来向我兜售的是一个人，他卖的是昂贵的钢笔和手表。
[01:38.10]I examined one of the pens closely. It certainly looked genuine. | 我仔细察看了一支钢笔，它看起来确实像真货。
[01:43.79]At the base of the gold cap, the words 'made in the U.S.A.' had been neatly inscribed. | 在金笔帽的底端，整齐地刻着“美国制造”的字样。
[01:52.31]The man said that the pen was worth ￡50, but as a special favour, he would let me have it for ￡30. | 那人说这支笔值50英镑，但作为特别优惠，他愿意让我出30英镑买下。
[02:02.21]I shook my head and held up five fingers indicating that I was willing to pay ￡5. | 我摇摇头，伸出5根手指表示我只愿出5英镑。
[02:10.51]Gesticulating wildly, the man acted as if he found my offer outrageous, | 那人拼命打着手势，仿佛我的出价使他无法容忍，
[02:17.42]but he eventually reduced the price to 10 pounds. | 但他终于把价钱降到了10英镑。
[02:22.62]Shrugging my shoulders I began to walk away when, | 我耸耸肩便走开了，
[02:26.62]a moment later, he ran after me and thrust the pen into my hands. | 一会儿工夫，他追了上来，把笔塞到了我手里。
[02:33.35]Though he kept throwing up his arms in despair, he readily accepted the ￡5 I gave him. | 虽然他绝望地连连挥动双臂，但他还是欣然接受了我付给他的5英镑。
[02:40.57]I felt especially pleased with my wonderful bargain--until I got back to the ship. | 我为这笔绝妙的交易得意洋洋——直到回到船上。
[02:47.77]No matter how hard I tried, | 无论我怎样摆弄，
[02:50.58]it was impossible to fill this beautiful pen with ink and to this day it has never written a single word! | 都无法把墨水灌进这支漂亮的钢笔。直到今天，它还一个字也没写过呢！
